-### SDM630 energy meter (`ENABLE_SDM_METER`)
+### SDM630 / DTS4921 energy meter (`ENABLE_SDM_METER`)
 
-Boards with an Eastron SDM630 / SDM72D-M (or compatible) meter on RS485 can read it over
+Boards with an Eastron SDM630 / SDM72D-M (or compatible) or a DTS4921 meter on RS485 can read it over
 Modbus RTU. Build flags: `ENABLE_SDM_METER`, `SDM_METER_SERIAL` (default `Serial2`),
 `SDM_METER_RX`, `SDM_METER_TX`, `SDM_METER_BAUD` (9600), `SDM_METER_ADDRESS` (1). The RS485
 transceiver must switch direction by itself. When the meter answers, `/status` reports its
 values: `amp`/`voltage` (L1), `power` (total), `amp2`, `amp3`, `voltage2`, `voltage3`,
-`phases` (phases above 1 A), `meter_import_kwh`, `meter_valid`, `meter_present`, `meter_errors`, and the session
-energy is integrated from the measured total power. If the meter does not answer for 30 s
-(box sold without meter), `meter_present` turns `false`, the controller values are used and the
-meter is only probed once a minute. `DEBUG_PORT_NULL` sends debug output only to
+`phases` (phases above 1 A), `meter_import_kwh`, `meter_valid`, `meter_present`, `meter_errors`,
+`meter_type` and `meter_serial`, and the session energy is integrated from the measured total power.
+If the meter does not answer for 30 s (box sold without meter), `meter_present` turns `false`, the
+controller values are used and the meter is only probed once a minute.
+
+The register map and the serial setting are detected at start and whenever the meter has not
+answered for 10 s. The driver reads L1 voltage with the SDM630 map first (input registers, IEEE-754
+float) and then with the native DTS4921 map; the first one that gives 100–300 V is kept and shown as
+`meter_type` (`sdm630` or `dts4921`, `unknown` before the first success). A wrong map answers with
+valid frames but nonsense (an integer read as float is close to 0 V) or with a Modbus exception.
+If the meter does not answer three times in a row (timeout or bad CRC), the other parity is tried:
+8N1 and 8E1 (`meter_serial`). The DTS4921 ships with address 1, 9600 baud, 8E1. The last working
+setting is tried first on the next detection. All values keep their units (V, A, W, kWh).
+
+| Value | SDM630 (float) | DTS4921 (32 bit, high word first) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Voltage L1-L3 | 0x0000/02/04 | 0x0100/02/04, uint32, 0.1 V |
+| Current L1-L3 | 0x0006/08/0A | 0x0106/08/0A, uint32, 0.001 A |
+| Power L1-L3 | 0x000C/0E/10 | 0x0110/12/14, int32, 0.1 W |
+| Total power | 0x0034 | 0x010E, int32, 0.1 W |
+| Import energy | 0x0048 | 0x0027, uint32, 0.01 kWh |
+| Total energy | 0x0156 | 0x001D, uint32, 0.01 kWh |
+
+Both maps are read with function 0x04. The driver never writes to the meter (on the DTS4921 a
+write to 0x0020 clears the energy counters, 0x0061–0x0063 change address, baud rate and parity).
+Framing, CRC and decoding are host-tested in `test/test_sdm_meter_proto`. `DEBUG_PORT_NULL` sends debug output only to
 the web console, for boards where UART0 is the RAPI link.
